      "message": "On builders not finding this when linking. It looks like this is defined with storage in `SkDebug_android.cpp` which is provided by `//src/ports:skdebug` which is referenced in `//src/ports:srcs` (old build) and `//src/ports:base_srcs` (new build). As a result, this should be part of `//src/base:base` (new build).\n\nThis file is in `//tools/testrunners/common:testrunner` which deps on `//:core` which does deps on `//src/base:base`. While this means `gSkDebugToStdOut` will be available, since there is no direct dependency on `base`, this target will not link against `base` and the linker will not know about the symbol. This is because the deps of `core` are not public but are implementation details and `core` could in theory change its list of dependencies at any time. I think the issue is solvable by adding a dependency to `//src/base` here.",
